 "method": [
  "one push is the unit: every workflow it starts runs at once, so the wall a developer waits for is the slowest run of the push, and the acceptance figure is the median over pushes",
  "before is the workflow tree at `before_ref`, measured; after is the same runs with the moved work removed from them \u2014 a workflow that left the pull-request set drops out of the maximum, a job that moved ends the run where the last kept job ended (the job's own measured clock), and a step that moved out of a surviving job is subtracted from that job's span",
  "green runs whose job payload the unauthenticated API did not give are counted at their measured wall and listed per push under `unpriced`; they are the cheap workflows, and none of them gained work",
  "wall time is `run_started_at` to the last kept job's `completed_at`, so time spent queued for a runner is included on both sides, exactly as `e11.1` measured it"
